# Spec: <change name>

**Status:** draft | ready | superseded
**Slug:** `<slug>`
**Last updated:** <date>

## Problem

What is wrong today, for whom, and what it costs. Two or three sentences. If you cannot
say who is affected, the change may not be needed.

## Goals

What must be true when this is done. Outcomes, not tasks.

## Non-goals

What this change explicitly does not do. Name the adjacent things a reader would
reasonably assume are included — this section exists to stop scope creep in review.

## Affected surface

What already exists and is being touched.

| Component | What changes | Consumers | Breaking? |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| | | | |

## Requirements

Numbered, testable, one behavior each.

- **R1.** …
- **R2.** …

## Edge cases

The inputs and states that are easy to forget. Empty, duplicate, concurrent, oversized,
out-of-order, unauthorized, partially migrated.

| Case | Expected behavior |
| --- | --- |
| | |

## Failure behavior

For each dependency this change relies on: what happens when it is unavailable, slow, or
returns something invalid — and what the caller sees.

| Dependency | On failure | Caller sees |
| --- | --- | --- |
| | | |

## Acceptance criteria

Observable facts that prove it works. Each maps to a requirement. Written so someone who
did not build it can verify it.

- [ ] **A1** (R1) …
- [ ] **A2** (R2) …

## Assumptions

Everything inferred rather than confirmed. Mark `(assumed)` until the user confirms.
Anything still assumed at sign-off moves to Open risks.

## Open risks

What could invalidate this spec, and what would resolve it.

## Policies touched

Generated by matching the triggers in `.brownspec/policies.md` against this spec, as a
separate pass after the spec was written. Each entry names the decision or confirmation
this spec still owes — not a restatement of the rule.

- **<RULE-ID>** (<short name>) — needs a decision: <what is unresolved>

**Not a compliance assessment.** Requires review by whoever owns security.

## Convention deviations

Where this change departs from `.brownspec/conventions.md`, and why. Empty is the normal
case.
